@page "/about"

@*
    Was a bare h1, and unreachable: its only link was in the branch of NavMenu that stopped being
    rendered once MainLayout got its own nav.

    Deliberately short. This page answers "what is this thing" for somebody who arrived from a
    stream or a search, and hands off to the pages that go further rather than repeating them.
*@

<div class="top-section">
    <div class="hero-text">
        <h1>About Ravenfall</h1>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="white-section-break"></div>

<div class="page-content">
    <div class="section">
        <div class="rf-prose">
            <p>
                Ravenfall is an idle role playing game that a Twitch streamer runs and their whole
                chat plays. The streamer installs the client; everyone else joins by typing
                <span class="rf-cmd">!join</span>. There is nothing for a viewer to download and
                nothing to sign up for.
            </p>
            <p>
                Characters carry on without you. You pick a skill to train and it keeps going while
                you watch something else, and the progress is yours: the same character plays on any
                channel running the game, so what you build on one stream comes with you to the
                next.
            </p>
            <p>
                Around that sit the things that make a chat play together rather than side by side.
                Raids and dungeons the whole stream joins at once. Clans that share a level everyone
                contributes to. A town per streamer whose plots boost a skill for everybody playing
                there. A marketplace where players trade with each other rather than with the game.
            </p>
            <p>
                It is free, and it stays free. The
                <a href="https://www.patreon.com/ravenfall" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Patreon</a>
                pays for the servers and gives patrons an experience multiplier and a few
                conveniences; <a href="/tiers">the tiers page</a> lists exactly what, and nothing
                there is unavailable to anyone else with time instead.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <h1>Where to go next</h1>
        <div class="rf-cards">
            <a class="rf-card" href="/how-to-play">
